# Review Note: Emergent Roles, Context Governance, and the Retirement of Symmetry-as-Principle

## TL;DR

Context governance should not be settled by upfront design. It should be resolved the same way every other system-level weakness is resolved: by evidence, through the system's own feedback loops — including the loop's ability to propose *new roles*, not merely tune existing ones. Recursive symmetry is downgraded from a design principle to an observed, opportunistic implementation convenience. Evaluation-model diversity is reframed from a current defect to a future experimental dimension.

> **Motto:** Don't pre-assign what evidence should discover.

## Status

This note records the outcome of a conceptual review pass conducted after the initial documentation set was drafted. It does not replace any existing document. It identifies where existing documents should evolve and why, ahead of a working session where the files themselves will be edited directly.

Three topics were addressed. Two others (memory promotion/authority, and the milestone sequence's own weight) were deliberately deferred to a later pass and are not covered here.

